## Slot vocabulary

The class declares **{{slot-count}}** slots covering:

- **Identity** — name, description, scope, memory-type
- **Provenance** — created, last-touched, last-reviewed, created-by, importance
- **Typed edges** — the full predicate vocabulary (cites, related, refines, evidences, etc.) — see the predicate memorials for per-predicate semantics
- **Structural** — body-raw, first-section (entry point of the section chain), links, frontmatter (long-tail extra keys)
- **Classification** — tags, themes
- **Origin tracking** — bootstrap-source, bootstrap-override (substrate-managed flags)

{{slot-table}}

## Canonical structure

A memorial markdown file:

```
---
<YAML frontmatter — slot values per the schema>
---

# Optional H1 heading (typically duplicates the `name:` field)

Body content as markdown — paragraphs, code blocks, headings (H2/H3
become substrate `:mm/Section` entities via the codec's section-tree
decomposition).

## Section heading

Section body content...

## See also

- Cross-reference links to other memorials
```

The codec at `sandbar.codec.markdown` handles the bidirectional translation between this filesystem form and substrate Datomic entities.  Round-trip stability is a substrate invariant — the normalized form is a fixed point under further round-trips.

## Composition with other classes

- **`:mm/Section`** — body decomposition.  Each H2+ heading becomes an addressable section entity with bidirectional sibling-chain navigation.
- **`:mm/Tag`** — classification.  Tags can be free-text (informal) or canonical (controlled-vocabulary via `:mm/ConceptScheme`).
- **`:mm/Link`** — markdown-link extraction.  Body content `[text](rel-path)` becomes a `:mm/Link` entity for backlink queries.
- **`:mm/Frontmatter`** — long-tail extra frontmatter keys.  Slots not declared on `:mm/Memory` can persist via `:mm.frontmatter/extra`.

